{"id": "2956ea17-6014-471d-9b81-fca2f7082641", "role": "assistant", "block_type": "thinking", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Worth checking if there are pending requests already, but that's optional. I should note the quota covers total aggregate IOPS across all io2 volumes in the region, so existing volumes count against it, and storage is capped at 20 TiB. I could offer to submit a Service Quotas increase request, which would need approval, and I should also flag that hitting the 256,000 per-volume max requires a Nitro instance.

For 150K IOPS, the volume needs sufficient size since io2 Block Express provides 1000 IOPS/GiB, so it'd need to be at least 150 GiB, and the instance type also has to support that level of EBS throughput.

